Upgrade procedure for tzdata

Source:	https://data.iana.org/time-zones/releases/tzdataVERSION.tar.gz
	https://data.iana.org/time-zones/releases/tzdataVERSION.tar.gz.asc
Key:	Paul Eggert <eggert@cs.ucla.edu>
	7E37 92A9 D8AC F7D6 33BC  1588 ED97 E90E 62AA 7E34

Vendor branch:	vendor/tzdata/dist
Vendor tag:	vendor/tzdata/dist/tzdataVERSION (e.g. tzdata2026f)
In-tree prefix:	contrib/tzdata
Last imported:	2026f

To upgrade to a new version:

1. Download the tarball and signature into an empty directory and
   verify with gpg.  Extract with --no-same-owner.
2. Use the vendor-update skill (vendor/tzdata/dist, contrib/tzdata).
   Nothing is pruned; the vendor branch is the whole tarball.
3. Subtree merge into master, build share/zoneinfo, and check a zone
   that changed with "zdump -v -c YEAR,YEAR ZONE".
4. Import tzcode of the same release when there is one (see
   contrib/tzcode) and add an UPDATING entry.

Local patches applied on top of upstream:

  - factory: the Factory zone abbreviation is
    "Local time zone must be set--use tzsetup" instead of "-00", as in
    FreeBSD, so an unconfigured system says what to do.
